{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T17:35:25.901Z","ordinal":35167,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a07234-4ad8-7891-917c-831f5a3a2228","turn_id":"01a08c63-1163-7d01-bcc4-c91a263dc8ee","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0e42ced9de323089016aa2ea4ef68c87d2b1f0887b8087e7b6","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The follow-up will clean **only the history of `codex/graph-advantage`**, preserving the final implementation and structured evidence.\n\n1. **Freeze the starting point.** Verify the remote tip against cleanup commit `e440b626`. Record the tree, removal-map digest, and protected branch/tag/checkpoint refs.\n\n2. **Make validation independent of deleted artifacts.** Some cleanup checks still read original archives from old commits. Replace those dependencies with compact, independent fixtures and committed provenance checks. Preserve coverage, ordering, failures, and original measurement identities. Commit and push this prerequisite normally.\n\n3. **Prepare exact historical cleanup lists.**\n   - Delete only the 1,385 paths recorded as removed in the final removal map.\n   - Separately list exact historical content changes needed to remove private paths and infrastructure identifiers from retained files.\n   - Exclude every file that existed before this branch. No broad directory or extension deletion rules.\n\n4. **Create verified external backups.** Save the original history and eight raw profiles outside the repository. Verify their hashes and test recovery before rewriting anything.\n\n5. **Rehearse in an isolated clone.** Rewrite only this branch’s commits after its baseline. Produce an old-to-new commit map. Preserve recorded measurement commit IDs as historical identities; do not relabel results.\n\n6. **Verify the proposed history.**\n   - Final tree must exactly match the approved prerequisite commit.\n   - Product code, fixtures, structured evidence, and pre-existing files must remain unchanged.\n   - All cleanup checks must pass in a fresh clone without the removed objects.\n   - Report actual object-size reduction and any artifacts still reachable through protected refs.\n\n7. **Present the result for your approval.** Show exact old/new branch tips, cleanup lists, validation results, backup details, and checkpoint implications. Preparation does not authorize a force-push.\n\n8. **Publish only if approved.** Update this branch with an explicit force-with-lease. Verify the remote tip and protected refs afterward. Keep the backup and commit mapping for recovery.\n\nCheaper-model subagents will handle preparation and independent verification; I will orchestrate and review. No benchmarks, implementation expansion, merge, or rewriting of other branches, tags, or Entire checkpoint history.\n\n**Limitation:** preserving other refs means some old objects may remain reachable. This cleans the branch’s history; it cannot guarantee repository-wide erasure."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1789061711008,"completed_at_ms":1789061725901}}
